#!RuleTest
#test FDA-SE2211 expect=violation domain=TS
#note "No TSPARMCD=SPECIES record anywhere in TS -> the 'Species' parameter is missing, one dataset-level finding. the related test-system parameters STRAIN / SBSTRAIN / SPFIND are present, so a prefix/substring match on the filter would wrongly silence the rule."
#library standard=sendig version=3-1-1
#expectViolationCount 1
dataset TS class="TRIAL DESIGN" label="Trial Summary"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col TSSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col TSPARMCD type=Char label="Trial Summary Parameter Short Name"
col TSPARM   type=Char label="Trial Summary Parameter"
col TSVAL    type=Char label="Parameter Value"
---
S01 | TS | 1 | STITLE | Study Title | 28-Day Repeat Dose Toxicity Study
S01 | TS | 2 | STRAIN | Strain/Substrain | SPRAGUE-DAWLEY
S01 | TS | 3 | SBSTRAIN | Strain/Substrain Details | CRL:CD(SD)
S01 | TS | 4 | SPFIND | Specific Pathogen Free Indicator | Y
